  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it or see a rendered frame, so lighting levels, the marble look and the camera sweep are untested. I picked the light intensities (spot 95, rim 0.9, fill 0.3) without being able to tune them by eye, so they may need adjusting.\n\n- **Pedestal:** Four stepped marble boxes. The marble is a procedural 512² texture built in code from layered noise, with turbulence-warped main veins, finer secondary veins and soft cloud haze. Three seeds give different patterns. The material is `material.physical` with clearcoat and low roughness, so it should look polished and pick up some room reflection.\n- **Trophy:** A lathe profile gives the foot, stem, knob and a flared hollow cup. Two tube handles are swept along Catmull-Rom curves. A darker, rougher gold band sits on the cup and another on the foot. A polished black stone base with a thin gold plate sits underneath. The gold is fully metallic with low roughness and a strong environment-reflection setting.\n- **Environment and lights:**\n  - The environment is `environments.neutral`, the engine's code-generated dark room with bright lamps. I used it because the engine's other environment sources need image files.\n  - The room has a floor, three walls, two glowing windows and two lamps with point lights.\n  - The key light is a warm shadow-casting spot, high and in front of the pedestal, with a wide soft edge for the falloff.\n  - There is a faint cool fill, a cool rim light and a little bloom.\n- **Camera:** A perspective camera pointed at the trophy, set each frame with `app.camera?.setPose`. It swings ±15° around the trophy's vertical axis. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame with the current azimuth, and `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n\nIf `app.camera` is undefined at runtime, the camera will stay fixed at its starting position instead of sweeping.\n\n",
